Optional private ROCm runtime
-----------------------------

When a machine has no HIP runtime, `./crucible setup` can download one into the install folder
(.crucible/rocm-runtime), only after you answer yes. The files are AMD software (the ROCm 10.1 runtime
from the rocm-sdk-core package on https://stable.repo.amd.com). They are not part of Crucible, and this
repository and the release files do not contain them. Setup checks each file against a sha256 pinned in
tools/crucible_cli/runtime-pin.json. Setup copies the license files that the AMD package holds into
.crucible/rocm-runtime/licenses/: ROCR-Runtime (NCSA), Comgr (Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions) and
rocprofiler-register (MIT). The package also holds the HIP runtime (MIT), LLVM and Clang
(Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions) and system libraries (libelf, libnuma, libdrm, zlib, bzip2, xz, zstd)
under their own licenses. The user receives these files from AMD, not from Crucible.
